The curve for the hotter globe should:

- have a **higher intensity at all wavelengths** (the total radiated power increases as $T^4$), so it lies above the original curve;
- have its **peak at a shorter wavelength** (to the left of $0.85\ \mu$m, since $\lambda_{max}\propto1/T$) and a higher peak;
- have the **absorption dips at the same wavelengths** as before, since they depend only on the hydrogen gas (about the same height).
